From 6e7aa76880fac5d770fb81228155f10996aea627 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael John <mj@tierone.software>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:50:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] nvi: fix error-path memory safety, leaks, and tiny-screen
 underwrites
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Memory safety:
- file_write()/msgq_status(): the long-path ellipsis logic underwrites
  the buffer by up to 3 bytes when sp->cols <= 2 (cols-3 wraps as
  size_t) — stack in exf.c, heap in msg.c, plus a wild pointer via
  p-(cols-5) for cols<5.  Reachable with a 2-column terminal (initial
  TIOCGWINSZ/SIGWINCH skips the :set columns minimum).  PoC-verified
  under ASan with a pty at cols=2: abort at startup (msg.c) and on :w
  (exf.c); both clean post-fix.
- Double-fclose/double-free on failed fclose in ex_readfp(),
  ex_writefp(), rcv_mailfile(): NULL the FILE* on the failed-fclose
  branch, guard the err close.
- argv_sexp() err path typo closed std_output[0] twice and leaked
  std_output[1]; now closes std_output[1].

Error-path leaks (long-lived editor; fire on DB/I/O errors):
- msgq_status() db_last failure now frees the scratch buffer (also
  unsticks G_TMP_INUSE); ex_move() six in-loop returns now goto an
  err tail that FREE_SPACEWs; file_write() db_last failure closes fp;
  ex_read() closes fp when fstat fails after fopen; argv_sexp()
  ferror/alloc-fail paths close ifp; ex_filter() second-fork failure
  uses fclose(ofp) instead of leaking the FILE; rcv_sync() no longer
  double-closes fd when close() itself fails; rcv_mailfile() err
  closes the dup'd rcv_fd; conv_enc() err closes the first iconv
  handle when the second open fails; ex_buildargv()/ex_tag_copy()/
  ex_at()/ex_global() free partial allocations on OOM; argv_flt_path()
  closedir()s on OOM.

Correctness:
- ex_readfp() sets *nlinesp (= lines actually read) on error paths;
  callers used the value unconditionally.
- v_delete() failure branch computes nlines lazily (was uninitialized
  on db_get failure).
- file_backup() checks the strdup.

All present verbatim in freebsd-src main (contrib/nvi).
Upstream patch queued as upstream-patches/0050.
